recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">finely chopped onion</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for flavor</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">clove</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">garlic, minced</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">adds rich taste</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Worcestershire sauce</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">brings umami flavor</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">salt</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">enhances overall taste</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/4</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">black pepper</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for a hint of spice</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/4</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">paprika</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">adds color and flavor</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">olive oil</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for grilling</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-6438-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"6438\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 grill or grill pan&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For grilling the patties</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 large bowl&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For mixing ingredients</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Spatula&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For flipping the patties</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-6438-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-6438-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"6438\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Instructions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6438-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">In a large bowl, combine ground chicken, breadcrumbs, egg, chopped onion, minced garlic, Worcestershire sauce, salt, pepper, and paprika.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6438-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Mix gently until all ingredients are evenly incorporated. Be careful not to overwork the meat!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6438-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Divide the mixture into 4 equal portions. Shape each portion into a patty about 1/2-inch thick.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6438-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Heat a grill or grill pan over medium-high heat. Brush the grates with olive oil to prevent sticking.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6438-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Place the patties on the grill. Cook for 5–6 minutes on each side. Ensure the internal temperature reaches 165°F (74°C) and the patties are golden brown.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6438-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Remove the patties from the grill. Let them rest for 2 minutes before serving. Enjoy your delicious grilled chicken patties!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-6438-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrition Facts</th>\n<th>Per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>250</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>12g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>30g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>10g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s what you’ll need to whip up some delicious grilled chicken <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patty\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">patties</a>!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Ingredients-for-Grilled-Chicken-Patties.webp\" alt=\"Ingredients for grilled chicken patties displayed on a kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-6436\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Ingredients-for-Grilled-Chicken-Patties.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Ingredients-for-Grilled-Chicken-Patties-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>1 lb ground chicken</strong> – the main protein base for the patties</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/4 cup breadcrumbs</strong> – helps bind the mixture</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 egg</strong> – adds moisture and binds ingredients</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 tablespoons finely chopped onion</strong> – for flavor</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 clove garlic, minced</strong> – adds rich taste</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 teaspoon Worcestershire sauce</strong> – brings umami flavor</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/2 teaspoon salt</strong> – enhances overall taste</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/4 teaspoon black pepper</strong> – for a hint of spice</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/4 teaspoon paprika</strong> – adds color and flavor</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tablespoon olive oil</strong> – for grilling</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-amazing-grilled-chicken-patties\"><strong>How to Make Amazing Grilled Chicken Patties</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to whip up some delicious grilled chicken patties! With a preparation time of 15 minutes and a cooking time of 12 minutes, these tasty treats are perfect for any meal. Don&#8217;t forget to let them rest for 2 minutes before serving!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/How-to-Make-Grilled-Chicken-Patties.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step process of making grilled chicken patties, including mixing ingredients, shaping patties, and grilling.\" class=\"wp-image-6437\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/How-to-Make-Grilled-Chicken-Patties.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/09/How-to-Make-Grilled-Chicken-Patties-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Combine Ingredients</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a large bowl, combine ground chicken, breadcrumbs, egg, chopped onion, minced garlic, Worcestershire sauce, salt, pepper, and paprika.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Mix Gently</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Mix gently until all ingredients are evenly incorporated. Be careful not to overwork the meat!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Shape Patties</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Divide the mixture into 4 equal portions. Shape each portion into a patty about 1/2-inch thick.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Heat the Grill</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Heat a grill or grill pan over medium-high heat. Brush the grates with olive oil to prevent sticking.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Grill the Patties</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Place the patties on the grill. Cook for 5–6 minutes on each side. Ensure the internal temperature reaches 165°F (74°C) and the patties are golden brown.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Let Rest</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Remove the patties from the grill. Let them rest for 2 minutes before serving. Enjoy your delicious grilled chicken patties!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Main Course</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>15 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>12 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>2 minutes (resting)</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>29 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>High Protein</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>With fresh toppings and sides!</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-grilled-chicken-patties\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making Grilled Chicken Patties</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Choose lean chicken breast for a healthier option.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Mix in breadcrumbs for a juicy texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Let the patties rest before grilling for better flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Preheat the grill to ensure a nice sear.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Experiment with spices to customize your taste.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-grilled-chicken-patties\"><strong>How to Serve this grilled chicken patties</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Serve on a toasted bun with fresh lettuce and tomato.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with avocado slices and a dollop of Greek yogurt for creaminess.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with a side of sweet potato fries for a delicious crunch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy with a refreshing cucumber and tomato salad for a light meal.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Make a grilled chicken patty wrap with your favorite veggies and hummus.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve alongside grilled corn on the cob for a summer vibe.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s how to keep your grilled chicken patties fresh and delicious:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow patties to cool completely.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place in an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Wrap each patty in plastic wrap.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place wrapped patties in a freezer bag.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and freeze for up to 3 months.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw in the refrigerator overnight if frozen.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reheat in a skillet over medium heat for 5-7 minutes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Alternatively, use a microwave for 1-2 minutes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Ensure internal temperature reaches 165°F (74°C).</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. Is grilled chicken patty healthy?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Absolutely! Grilled chicken patties are a great source of lean protein, which is essential for muscle building and overall health. They are typically lower in fat compared to fried options, especially if you use skinless chicken. Plus, you can customize them with healthy ingredients like herbs and spices to enhance their nutritional value.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. Can you put chicken patties on the grill?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Yes, you can definitely put chicken patties on the grill! In fact, grilling is one of the best methods to cook chicken patties as it adds a delicious smoky flavor and helps to keep them juicy. Just make sure your grill is preheated and lightly oiled to prevent sticking.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. What is the best way to cook chicken patties?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>The best way to cook chicken patties is to grill them, as it allows for even cooking and a nice char. However, you can also pan-fry or bake them if you prefer. Just ensure they reach an internal temperature of 165°F (75°C) for safe consumption. Whichever method you choose, be sure to season them well for maximum flavor.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. How do you avoid rubbery grilled chicken patties?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>To avoid rubbery grilled chicken patties, make sure not to overcook them. Use ground chicken that has some fat content, as this helps keep the patties moist. Additionally, consider marinating the chicken beforehand or adding ingredients like breadcrumbs or finely chopped vegetables to the mixture to enhance texture and flavor.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Now that you have the recipe for these amazing grilled chicken patties, it’s time to fire up the grill and enjoy! Picture a sunny day, laughter with friends, and the delicious aroma wafting through the air. Simple, satisfying, and oh-so-rewarding, these patties are sure to become a favorite. Happy grilling!</p>\n",
